[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Technical Tutorial: Increment, Definition of Done, and Shippable Quality in Scrum"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"In Scrum, the Increment is the concrete stepping stone toward the Product Goal. Each Increment is additive to all prior increments and thoroughly verified, ensuring that all increments work together. To deliver true value, the Increment must meet the Definition of Done (DoD)."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding the Scrum Increment"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"An Increment is a functional piece of software or deliverable product that is usable and inspectable at the end of a Sprint. It represents the sum of all the Product Backlog items completed during the Sprint and the value of the increments of all previous Sprints."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"The Role of the Definition of Done (DoD)"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Definition of Done is a formal description of the state of the Increment when it meets the quality measures required for the product. The moment a Product Backlog item meets the Definition of Done, an Increment is born."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code review completed and approved by peers."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automated unit and integration tests passing successfully."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Security vulnerabilities scanned and resolved."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Deployed to the staging or production environment."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Achieving Shippable Quality"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Shippable quality does not necessarily mean the product is released to customers immediately. Instead, it means that the Increment is completely finished, robust, and safe to deploy at the Product Owner's discretion without requiring further technical work."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"// Example pipeline check representing automated Definition of Done criteria
stage('Quality Gate') {
    steps {
        sh 'npm run test:unit'
        sh 'npm run lint'
        sh 'sonar-scanner'
    }
}"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Scrum Teams"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Make the Definition of Done visible and transparent to the entire organization."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Evolve the DoD over time as the team's technical maturity and product architecture grow."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Never compromise quality for velocity; incomplete items cannot be part of the Increment."}]
